The family also brought a little dog on the train.
It was very cute, but it was not quiet.
The dog lay in its little basket on the floor.
The father looked down at his book again.
He just wanted to read a little.
But suddenly the dog jumped out of its basket.
It ran quickly over to the father.
He sat with one foot up on a bag.
The dog grabbed his left shoe.
It took the shoe in its mouth.
Then it ran away quickly.
"No, come back with my shoe!" the father shouted.
He stood up in his socks.
He ran after the dog down the aisle.
The two children pointed at him.
They looked at each other and laughed loudly.
I looked at them from my seat.
I also laughed a little behind my book.
Fortunately, he finally caught his dog.
He also got his shoe back.
